{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "000Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{Cov}(\\mathcal{C})_\\alpha$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sets-section-reflection-principle}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sets-remark-how-to-use-reflection}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{sets-remark-better}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{remark}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfee37ce4b9f55efb6d7a7722f698ebcc0b5da0c0f6befc6a4b5d62501905d62", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8ccf05189aebf884d7ce34a2caed92fc90d893b0ad5900b59755eea0a34d3979", "source_text": "It is likely the case that, for some limit ordinal <MATH_0001>, the set of coverings <MATH_0002> satisfies the conditions of the lemma. This is after all what an application of the reflection principle would appear to give (modulo caveats as described at the end of Section <REF_0001> and in Remark <REF_0002>).", "source_text_hash": "sha256:25638dc9d8a6fa0ede7f99acff84301cc2b1aba4173f3b2351f8cf8fa6a7a1bf", "unit_id": "tag:000Y"}
